+## Board Publication
+
+Only account admins (including owners) can publish or unpublish a board they can access. Being the board's creator does not grant this permission.
+
+### `POST /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/publication`
+
+Publishes the board. No request parameters are required.
+
+Returns `201 Created` with the board in the same shape as `GET /:account_slug/boards/:board_id`, including its `public_url`. The `Location` header points to that public URL. Repeating the request preserves the existing URL.
+
+### `DELETE /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/publication`
+
+Unpublishes the board and revokes its public URL, including direct links to its columns and cards.
+
+Returns `204 No Content`. The board's `public_url` becomes `null`. Publishing it again generates a new secret URL; old links remain invalid.
+
+### Public pages
+
+These read-only HTML pages do not require authentication:
+
+- `GET /public/boards/:key`
+- `GET /public/boards/:key/columns/:id`
+- `GET /public/boards/:key/cards/:number`
+
+Only published cards are visible; drafts cannot be opened or listed. Columns and cards must belong to the board identified by the secret key. Invalid or revoked links return `404 Not Found`.
+
+Treat the public URL as a secret: anyone who has it can view the board. Publication does not change account membership or board access permissions. Publication keys are not included in account exports, and imported boards start unpublished.
+
 ## Board Accesses
 
 Board accesses let you see who has access to a board and their involvement level (watching or access only). Any board member can view this information.
